      "description": "The golden-single-small signature integer s replaced by the noncanonical representative s+n (still k=256 bytes: the golden's top byte 0x11 cannot overflow the octet length over the 0xc2-prefixed 2048-bit modulus). RSAVP1 (RFC 8017 \u00a75.2.2 step 1) rejects any signature representative outside [0, n-1], and \u00a78.2.2 step 2b maps \u201csignature representative out of range\u201d to an invalid signature, so verification MUST return false. A verifier that feeds s straight into modular exponentiation would reduce s+n modulo n back to the golden's representative and wrongly accept; the verdict pins the range check as part of RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 verification itself \u2014 the JCA SunRsaSign and BouncyCastle verifiers both return false for such representatives.",
